KZ3 patch 2213 (RSX pass 176): LD_SMP_RING_NODRAIN=1 (default off; 2 = also count tables without a fence at the wrap): a full sampler ring wraps without draining the queue.

Cause (read from the code and the profiling logs, NOT run in the game): flush_other in [perf-split-w] is the full-queue drain of the draw path when the sampler descriptor ring (128 tables x 16 samplers, the D3D12 2048-sampler heap limit) is full and the draw's table is new: sampler_table_needs_flush -> ld_rm_try_wrap fails (LD_RING_FENCE_WAIT off) -> ld_flush(LD_FLUSH_DESCRIPTOR_RING), a Signal+wait of the fence just submitted, which also absorbs the whole GPU backlog (queue is in order). Evidence: [perf-flush] 'wraps smp N' equals 'descring' flush count in all three series-1123 logs (probe-g2 295/295, p1 157/157, a1 206/206); srv/up/vtx/cb/pscb wraps 0; no [ld-ring] line (switch off). flush_other 0.3-1.9 ms/flip at 0.27-0.67 waits/flip in the sampled [perf-split-w] lines (the 3-4 ms seen earlier is the per-wait cost).

Why not just LD_RING_FENCE_WAIT=1: its marks (patch 2155 rsx_rm_submit_live) keep the whole allocated prefix live through every submit, so after a wrap the first reuse waits for the fence of the submit that closed the wrap = the drain again, and it also wraps the SRV ring. This patch uses exact per-table stamps instead: sampler_table() is called once per draw (hit or take) and the table is read only by that draw's list (root table set directly, no memo), so rsx_smp_use.h marks a table UNSUB when a draw of the open list binds it, ld_rm_note_submit (the common submit hook, all three submit paths) turns UNSUB into the submit's fence, and ld_smp_take waits for the newest binding fence of the table it overwrites (fence value cached, GetCompletedValue only when needed; the wait goes through ld_wait_fence_s site RING, so [perf-split-w] ring and the RFW_DESC_WAIT/AVOID perf counters stay truthful).

Change: rsx_live_draw.c draw path: when only the sampler ring is full and the switch is on, ld_smp_wrap_nodrain() (ld_oq_close + ld_submit_nowait; an open query falls back to the old drain, counted) replaces the drain and only g.smp_ring_used is reset; the SRV ring and g_srv_desc_gen are left alone. Not combined with LD_RING_FENCE_WAIT=1 (that path keeps its own marks). rsx_smp_use.h is new and pure. Fail closed: a failed fence wait returns LD_TAKE_FAIL as patch 2157 does. A table still UNSUB when it is about to be overwritten (a ring reset without a submit, as ld_movie_reset_rings) has no fence: counted (unfenced_at_take), no wait, same as the old code.

Expected effect: the descring drain disappears; the walker still waits at the first takes after the wrap if the GPU has not reached the chunk that last bound table k (bounded above by the old drain). Estimate 0.3-1.9 ms/flip walker time at K4, ~+0.5..2 fps if walker-bound. Verify in a run: [perf-flush] descring ~0 with 'wraps smp' unchanged, [ld-ring] smp-nodrain wraps>0, fallback=0, unfenced_at_wrap=0 (LD_SMP_RING_NODRAIN=2), unfenced_at_take small, flush_other and ring waits in [perf-split-w], and a pixel-identical screenshot against the off side. Host test: tools/smoke/test_smp_nodrain.sh.

